  "description": "Document-tier (Azure Cosmos DB) reliability provider for Chatter.MessageBrokers: the DI surface, document-tier reliability surface (atomic-write handle over TransactionalBatch), partition-key resolver, and the outermost batch-lifecycle behavior. Outbox enqueue, inbox dedup (co-resident inbox-marker with marker-409 confirmed-duplicate handling), and the change-feed outbox relay are implemented; Chatter exclusively owns the reserved inbox:/outbox: item-id namespace on the public staging surface. The relay drains _chatterType=outbox/status=pending documents (one ChangeFeedProcessor per distinct database/container/lease), publishes each through the broker, then marks delivered and stamps a TTL; it is at-least-once (downstream consumers dedup via the inbox marker) and requires the container to have defaultTtl enabled for post-delivery purge. AddCosmosOutboxRelay registers a standalone relay as its own IHostedService, independent of the command pipeline, for applications that drain a container without participating in AddChatterCqrs/WithCosmosDocumentReliability. IOutboxBodyResolver provides a drain-time body-resolution seam: the relay invokes the bound resolver per pending document so the brokered-message body can be sourced from current store state rather than reconstructed verbatim from the persisted outbox document.",
